# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored; nothing here may be committed with real
# values. gen-signing.sh reads this and writes Local.xcconfig, which Build.xcconfig
# already includes — so no tracked file ever carries a signing identity.

# Your signing identity, exactly as shown by:
#   security find-identity -v -p codesigning
# "Apple Development: …" for local dev builds, "Developer ID Application: …" to make a
# build that opens on another Mac. Leave unset entirely to build ad-hoc ("-"), which
# works for everything except capabilities that need a provisioning profile.
SIGN_IDENTITY="Apple Development: Your Name (XXXXXXXXXX)"

# Your 10-character Apple Developer Team ID — the parenthetical on the
# "Developer ID Application" line above (an Apple Development line shows a certificate
# ID there, not the team).
DEV_TEAM="TEAMID"

# Selects MarkEditMac/Info$(ENTITLEMENTS_VARIANT).entitlements and the QuickLook
# equivalent. Leave empty to use the tracked Info.entitlements. Set to ".local" once you
# have registered the app group on developer.apple.com and want a gitignored
# Info.local.entitlements to carry it. That file stays untracked because the capabilities
# in it only work against one developer account's provisioning profiles.
ENTITLEMENTS_VARIANT=""
